0..79 Comment "//! A flow between types written as the relation `A ⇝ B`, also `A ~~> B`: the"
80..159 Comment "//! type-level spelling of `Flow(Type, A, B)`, introduced by `Flow.into` over a"
160..236 Comment "//! translator. Under directed univalence a flow between types is a function"
237..308 Comment "//! [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory],"
309..388 Comment "//! Definition 1.2, so `⇝` abbreviates the flow itself and no record of round"
389..416 Comment "//! trips stands beside it."
417..420 Comment "//!"
421..500 Comment "//! - cites: [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory]"
